A||N||11||007DOUG||Battery exploded (weird)......Any Ideas?||||1||
Z||000000||007DOUG||11-05-2000||10:56 PM||||This is my 84 4 banger, automatic. My daily fiero. Driven in stop-and-go traffic all day, idles for long periods of time too.<P>About three months ago, I shut the engine off for 5 minutes. I had to be jump started. The battery was fully charged. The only sound you could hear was the relay on the firewall. Not even the solenoid clicking. It took the power of two batteries to start the car?????<P>Everything has been fine till tonight. While driving I could hear the alternator whine through the radio REALLY bad. It was charging just fine. I shut the car off for 5 minutes, and had to be jumped. Assuming it was a bad battery, (The battery is old, and this problem hadn't happen for three months now) I replaced it with a known good one. <P>Everything is fine for the next few hours: No whine, No need for jumpstarts again.<P>Everything WAS fine until.......at the exact moment I turn the key "BANG", I blew a hole in the side of the battery. Even more weird is the fiero still starts with a hole in the battery.<P>My question: Whats wrong? <BR>Alternator?<BR>Starter?<BR>Battery?<P>All of the above STILL work.||||reg||1
Z||000001||007DOUG||11-05-2000||10:58 PM||||Forgot to mention, the starter/solenoid and positive cable are two years old. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||11-05-2000||11:04 PM||||Sound alternator-ish to me. If you happen to have a voltage tester, hook it up to the battery and see how many volts are being passed. I would advise you to hook the voltage tester to the battery and then start the car, then slowly creep up on the side of the car and peek at the reading. It should not be over about 15-16 volts, if it is, replace the alternator. Could be a faulty battery also, but it sounds to me like overcharging.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif">   <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>If you smoke after sex, your doing it way to fast.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000003||007DOUG||11-05-2000||11:09 PM||||At idle: 13.8-14.2 <P>In gear, foot an brake: 12.8<P>Highway cruizin: 13.8 dead even<P>The battery exploded the instant the car started.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-05-2000||11:19 PM||||Ignore the dash gauge and have the charging system checked with a profesional grade diagnostic tool. An over charging system or worse a system with a diode problem in the alt can cook batteries.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||MrPBody||11-05-2000||11:28 PM||||My guess is: battery.  I have seen -- well, heard -- batteries explode, probably because a spark inside the battery ignited hydrogen gas, which is normally present in the battery.<P>Electrochemistry in action.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Like Apollo 13.<P>Why did an spark occur inside your battery?  Probably a loose internal connection, which arced under load when you tried to start your car.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||HAGS||11-06-2000||01:28 AM||||You can hear things through the radio??  One day I was sitting at a red light and my engine died...when I tried to restart it I got a loud screach in the speakers, then I tried again and it started with no problem...that was back when my belts were loose and having battery problems.||||reg||5
Z||000007||Old Lar||11-06-2000||07:40 AM||||I hope you cleaned all the spilled battery acid from the inside of the engine compartment.  The battery tray will dissolve with the acid.<P>Something shorted in the battery spark + H2 gas = boom! as MrPBody stated.||||reg||1
Z||000008||deceler8||11-06-2000||09:16 AM||||Also be sure your battery is tight in the tray and not hitting the water pump pulley.<P>That's an easy way to put a hole in your battery...happened to me.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Xtreme Fiero's||11-06-2000||12:54 PM||||I have Blown the (+) post out of the batt. before Due to drawing way to much curent, And a few of my friends have done the same. since it juat started all of the acc's had just come back on that may have done it or a short in the + cable Before a fuseable link.||||reg||1
Z||000010||88formula||11-06-2000||04:49 PM||||I think the battery had a small crack in it usually caused by the terminals being tightened too much. Hydrogen gas than escaped through this crack and when you went to start your car a small spark ignited the hydrogen gas and bam your battery explodes. You are lucky because this usually happens when someone tries to jump-start the car with the hood open and you standing right in front of the battery. The acid from a battery will take your face off.||||reg||1
Z||000011||88formula||11-06-2000||05:03 PM||||Oh, and the reason why your car probably wont start intermittently is because you may have a loose connection at the battery terminals, starter, or ground. I know you have replaced them but it could still happen. Place a voltmeter across the positive and than the negative cables from one end to the other and read the voltage drop. It should not exceed .02 volts if I remember right. You have to do this while someone cranks over the starter at the same time so you will have to disable the ignition. You may also have a faulty starter solenoid. Easy way to check that is the next time this happens just jump the solenoid with jumper cables and see if the starter works. Make sure you have battery voltage though before you do anything and keep the sparks away from the battery.||||reg||1
